This license covers the Shaderera engine: the packages `@shaderera/core` (packages/core),
`shaderera` (apps/cli) and `@shaderera/registry` (apps/registry), and everything else in
this repository that is not listed under "MIT-licensed parts" below.

1. Free use

   You may use, copy, modify and run the Shaderera engine, and make and distribute videos and
   other works with it, free of charge, if you are:
   (a) an individual;
   (b) a for-profit organisation with 3 or fewer employees (counting contractors who work for it
       full time);
   (c) a non-profit organisation, or a school, university or other educational institution; or
   (d) anyone evaluating the engine, for up to 30 days, without using its output commercially.

2. Company license

   Any other organisation needs a company license from the Shaderera copyright holders to use the
   engine. An organisation that grows past the limit in 1(b) needs one from that time on.

3. Your work is yours

   Whatever you make with the engine (your project's source code, the videos and images it
   renders, and their sound) belongs to you. This license places no condition on it.

4. What you may not do

   You may not sell, sublicense, or offer as a service the engine itself or a modified copy of
   it, or remove this license from copies of it, except as a company license allows.

5. No warranty

   THE ENGINE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT
   NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
   NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
   DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
   OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE ENGINE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE ENGINE.

MIT-licensed parts

The following are under the MIT License (LICENSE-MIT), so that what they put into your project
is freely yours to change and share:
- `create-shaderera` (packages/create-shaderera) and the starter project it copies (packages/create-shaderera/project);
- the official registry items (packages/catalog/), except fonts, which keep their own licences (OFL 1.1);
- the agent skills and the Claude Code plugin (plugins/shaderera/).

Third-party code and assets keep their own licences; see docs/licences.md.
